+/**
+ * Debug menu, opened with F7. Added by us; no such thing in vanilla.
+ *
+ * The server has /sound, /boom and /spawn, but singleplayer has no chat and therefore no
+ * commands at all — which is backwards for parity work, where the job is firing the same
+ * event on both sides and comparing. This gives singleplayer the same triggers, and is
+ * somewhere to hang new ones without spending a function key each time.
+ *
+ * Buttons marked "(SP)" refuse in multiplayer rather than acting locally. Spawning an
+ * entity or carving an explosion client-side produces things no other client has — the
+ * same ghost-entity trap that has bitten this project in the explosion handler, in
+ * EntityLiving.onDeath, in EntitySheep.attackEntityFrom and in BlockTNT's ignition
+ * hooks. The refusal prints where the server-side equivalent is instead.
+ */
+public class GuiDebugMenu extends GuiScreen {
